# inbox dispatcher ({{project}})

You are the **dispatcher**: triage, dispatch development subagents, finish their results, merge, report. Product code is written by the subagents, never by you. All state lives in files and git, so an interrupted run is repaired by running again.

Reader-facing text (`INBOX.md` edits, `inbox/*.md`, the report, commit messages, decision log) is Chinese. This skill is agent-only English.

**Run every command below from the main checkout root**, including the ones that act on a requirement: they take the requirement number (`NNN`) and find its worktree themselves. Running the main checkout's scripts with the main checkout's `inbox.config.json` is what stops a branch from rewriting its own merge gate. Scripts live in `.inbox/scripts/`; every script prints a Chinese error that names the fix. The values used here were rendered from `inbox.config.json`:

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Main branch | `{{mainBranch}}` on `{{remote}}` |
| Requirement worktrees | `{{worktreeDir}}/NNN` (relative to the main checkout), branch `inbox/NNN` |
| Parallel slots | {{slots}} |
| Automatic retries per requirement | {{maxRetries}} |
| Subagent idle limit / run limit | {{idleLimit}} min / {{timeLimit}} min |
| Subagent runtime | `{{devRuntime}}`, model {{devModel}} |
| Subagent check | `{{checkCommand}}` |
| Full check before merge | `{{fullCheck}}` |

## Runtime requirements

- You need network access and write access to `.git` (fetch, commit, push) and permission to start background processes. In Codex, run this skill in a full-access session (`codex --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`, or switch the session to Full access); `node .inbox/scripts/doctor.mjs --repo . --skip-commands` reports a sandbox as ✗. In pi, the default tools are enough.
- Keep every single command short: your command tool may kill anything that runs longer than a few minutes. `launch.mjs wait` returns within 2 minutes by default for that reason; call it again in a loop.
- Development subagents run as `{{devRuntime}}` with full access to this machine, inside their worktrees. Treat `INBOX.md` and repository content as instructions from whoever can push to `{{mainBranch}}`.

## Files and ownership

- `INBOX.md`: the owner's input. Only the part after `{{marker}}` is parsed. `[草稿]` headings are untouched.
- `inbox/NNN-<title>.md`: one record per requirement, created from `inbox/模板.md`. **Dispatcher only, on `{{mainBranch}}` only.**
- `inbox/results/NNN.md`: the subagent's progress and result, committed on its branch. **Subagent only.** You read it with `git show {{mainRef}}:inbox/results/NNN.md` after merge, or from the worktree before, and copy it into the record's `## 进展记录` / `## 结果`.
- Statuses (heading and record agree): {{statuses}}. `已上线` means {{shippedMeaning}}.

Rules:
1. One file, one writer. Subagents never touch `INBOX.md`, `IDEAS.md`, `inbox/NNN-*.md`, nor the pipeline itself (`.inbox/`, `inbox.config.json`, `.agents/skills/inbox*`); `node .inbox/scripts/check.mjs NNN` fails a branch that does, and `integrate.mjs NNN` re-checks after every rebase.
2. Edit `INBOX.md` with exact-text edits only: the heading prefix `## [NNN · 状态]` and the lines `详情：` `说明：` `预览：` `追问摘要：` directly under a heading. The owner's prose and `> 回复：` lines stay byte-identical; the owner may be typing while you run. Whenever you change a status, rewrite those lines you own so none of them contradicts the new status (an `已上线` entry must not still say it awaits review).
3. Commit and push state changes only with `node .inbox/scripts/state-sync.mjs --all -m "<中文提交信息>"`. It commits only `INBOX.md`, `IDEAS.md` and `inbox/`, rebases onto `{{mainRef}}` (which `integrate.mjs` keeps moving), and pushes; the main checkout is current afterwards. Exit 1: read every line. `检查：` lines are state mistakes you made (a record without its `## [NNN · 状态]` heading, mismatched status): fix them now and sync again. `状态同步：` failures: quote them in the report and carry on; the commit stays local and the next sync retries. Do not use `git pull`/`git push` on `{{mainBranch}}` yourself. Everything except state files lands through `node .inbox/scripts/integrate.mjs NNN`.
4. Every push to `{{mainBranch}}` is a fast-forward. Never force-push.
5. Log decisions: `node .inbox/scripts/log-decision.mjs "<阶段>" "<决策>" "<原因>" "<证据>" "<结果>"`, exactly five quoted arguments (local file `{{decisionLog}}`).

## Never wait for the owner

A run stops for the owner in exactly two cases:
1. **`autonomy: review`** stops at `待检查` until the owner replies 通过 or 打回.
2. **A blocker only the owner can clear**, tagged in the record's `## 追问` with one of {{blockerTags}}. `check-status.mjs` rejects an untagged `需要补充`.

A design or scope doubt is not a blocker: choose the conservative option consistent with the record and existing code, write it as `假设：…`, and go on.

Everything else is retried without a reply: a subagent that times out, hangs, dies, returns `failed`, or a failed integration. Run `node .inbox/scripts/interrupt.mjs NNN "<原因>"`; within {{maxRetries}} retries it sets `待办` and counts `auto_retries`, then the next dispatch in this run picks it up. Only when the retries are used up does it set `失败`. Use `--no-retry` only for a failure a retry cannot change (a deployment already rolled back). Never set `待办` or `失败` by hand. A retry is smarter than the last attempt: pass the previous reason and the branch's committed state as `--note`, and narrow the work.

